# inc-q3r5: real AI-selected Watery Double attempt; seed 20260905.
# Covers the fourth removal path: loss of the MONSTER CASTER. The nereid
# is killed with a self-learned Disintegrate once the double has appeared,
# while the target (giant tortoise) and the bystander (pony) are both
# still alive -- so any collapse observed here is caused by the caster's
# death, not the target's (that path is watery-death.keys) and not
# duration expiry (that path is watery-expire.keys).
@include chargen.keys
w
y
ESC
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT ENTER
TAB
@choose "shallow water"
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Reptiles"
@choose "giant tortoise"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:target
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Quadrupeds"
@choose "pony"
LEFT*4 ENTER
@dump:bystander
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Faerie"
@choose "nereid"
RIGHT*3 ENTER
.
@dump:nereid
w
@choose "Make Player Master of Monster"
@until "A nereid" RIGHT
@dump:master-picked
ENTER
w
@choose "Add Template to Creature"
@until "A nereid" RIGHT
@expect "A nereid"
ENTER
@choose "paragon"
@expect "Template added."
@dump:before-wait
.
@dump:wait-1
.
@dump:wait-2
.
@dump:wait-3
.
@dump:wait-4
@expect "B aqueous giant"
@expect "B giant"
@expect "q pony"

# Kill the CASTER now, while the target and the bystander are both still
# alive. A self-targeted Disintegrate (as in watery-caster-death.keys)
# would end the game here, since the caster is the player in that
# fixture; here the caster is the nereid, so target it instead.
#
# The paragon nereid has 50% magic resistance and a boosted Fortitude
# save, so one ray is not reliable. At seed 20260905, deterministically:
# the first ray is turned aside ("The nereid resists your magic."), and
# the second gets through and fails the nereid's save (a paragon-boosted
# +6 base, 11 vs DC 19). Do NOT recast a third time: at this seed the
# nereid is already dead by then, and Disintegrate on its corpse item
# throws an engine error ("Invalid object reference (object type
# mismatch) calling GetAttr in script routine $"Disintegrate"::
# EV_MAGIC_STRIKE") -- a separate, pre-existing defect this fixture does
# not exercise or fix. Two casts is the deterministic kill at this seed.
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Disintegrate" ENTER
@dump:learned-disintegrate

m
@choose "Disintegrate"
@dump:kill-target-prompt
PGUP
@dump:kill-target-picked
@expect "A nereid"
ENTER
@dump:after-cast-1
@expect "resists your magic"
@expect "B aqueous giant"
@expect "f nereid"

m
@choose "Disintegrate"
PGUP
ENTER
@dump:after-nereid-death
@expect "The nereid disintegrates!"
@expect "aqueous giant tortoise collapses back to"
@expect "inanimate water!"
@expect "B giant"
@expect "q pony"

v
@dump:kill-messages
@expect "The nereid disintegrates!"
@expect "aqueous giant tortoise collapses back to"
@expect "inanimate water!"
ESC
.
@dump:wait-5
.
@dump:wait-6
.
@dump:wait-7
.
@dump:wait-8
.
@dump:wait-9
.
@dump:wait-10
v
@dump:cast-messages
